**`txtar/archive.go`** — `Lookup` method on `*Archive`:
```go
// Lookup returns the file with the given name, or nil and false if no such file exists.
func (a *Archive) Lookup(name string) (*File, bool) {
	for i := range a.Files {
		if a.Files[i].Name == name {
			return &a.Files[i], true
		}
	}
	return nil, false
}
```

**`txtar/archive_test.go`** — `TestLookup` covering both the found and not-found cases.

Key detail: I used index-based iteration (`for i := range a.Files`) instead of value iteration (`for _, f := range a.Files`) so the returned `*File` points directly into `a.Files`, allowing callers to modify the archive's file data through the returned pointer.

